    <item>
      <title>1D Transient Heat Conduction FDM.</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/project/1d-transient-heat-conduction-fdm/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 28 Sep 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/project/1d-transient-heat-conduction-fdm/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;This project simulates the 1D transient heat conduction in a rod using the explicit Finite Difference Method (FDM). The code is implemented in Python and visualizes the temperature distribution over space and time using three different plots- a 2D line plot, a heatmap, and a 3D surface plot. The user can choose an initial condition for the temperature distribution, and the boundary conditions are fixed at zero for both ends of the rod.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    
